<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Viken</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Viken was the medieval name for the lands around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslofjord">Oslofjord</a> and along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skagerrak">Skagerrak</a> coast, from modern Vestfold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostfold">Østfold</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohuslan">Bohuslän</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Danish kings claimed overlordship of it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>, and it was contested between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> into the 11th century before becoming firmly Norwegian. The name was revived for a Norwegian county that existed from 2020 to 2023.</p></div>
